WEBVTT

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.890
If I was going to a deserted island,
I would take...

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.640
One, Hana. Two, a book.
And three, a laptop.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.850
I think I would take...

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.480
One, a knife. Two, a tent.
And three, waterproof matches.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.690
What about me?

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.280
You're afraid of bugs,
so you would be totally worthless.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.700
You're kidding. Take me with you!

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.580
<i>THE LIFE AND ADVENTURES OF ROBINSON CRUSOE</i>

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:50.750
Arashi.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.920
Good morning.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.630
Good morning, Ms. Iwashimizu.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.800
Is that <i>Robinson Crusoe</i>?

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.640
Yes, I found it in my bag.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.430
I'm not sure who put it there.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:04.020
Is that so?

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.810
Hey, everybody. Can you come here?

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.310
Sounds like Ms. Botan wants us. Let's go.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:16.070
<i>Since we heard about the project,
even Arashi has been down in the dumps.</i>

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.160
I sketched a quick map.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.120
LIGHT SNOW

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.960
I think we should climb up
the highest mountain to get a better view.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.390
It's slippery here. Watch your step.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.190
What a klutz.
She just told us to watch our step.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.690
Nat, that's pretty careless.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.200
You may think being clumsy and ditsy
looks cute to guys,

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.660
but out here, it will cost you your life.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.660
<i>I don't think that at all.</i>

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:27.740
Get with the program.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.080
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.500
<i>I get the feeling that the only thing
on Arashi's mind is his girlfriend.</i>

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:40.720
<i>He didn't even ask me if I'm okay
like he did before.</i>

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.180
You're waiting for someone to ask
if you're okay, aren't you?

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.640
Stop being such a princess.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.020
If you want to take a break,
speak up for yourself.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.770
<i>She's reading me like a book.</i>

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.020
I'm fine.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.270
Really? Then hang in there.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.030
Help!

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.950
I heard someone shouting.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.160
What is it, Nat?

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.410
I thought I heard someone just now.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.160
Jeez, don't start making stuff up
just to take a break.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.250
Somebody, help!

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:17.750
There's someone down there!

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.920
What the hell is that?

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:19.840
What?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.840
All your yelling
really did make a difference.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:22.760
Help us, please!

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.630
Can't you climb up from over there?

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:26.800
The mud makes it too slippery!

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.890
Now is your chance! Move!

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:33.890
Got it!

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.610
Take my hand!

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:39.860
Are you okay?

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.360
Yes, thanks so much.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:43.610
Who are you?

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.570
Oh, let me introduce myself.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.120
I'm Matsuri Tendo. I'm 16 years old.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.040
Chimaki Yamori.
I'm a freshman in an art college.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.920
My name is Hotaru Kusakari. I'm 12.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.330
I see.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.500
Then you must be
the remaining members of our group.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.260
Now, all members of Team Summer B
are together.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.260
Man, I'm starving. Let's get some food.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.180
Right.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.310
Before that, there's something important
I need to explain to you three,

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.270
regarding the reason why we're all here.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.440
<i>Why did they pick someone like me?</i>

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.820
<i>They should have chosen someone useful,</i>

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.370
<i>someone stronger, with actual skills.</i>

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.580
Grandma always used to give me
a hard time.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.660
She called me clumsy.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:39.840
<i>That harbor in Grandma's hometown
always reeked of fish.</i>

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.750
I hate the ocean because it stinks so bad.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:49.260
Wait!

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:50.680
What are you doing?

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:59.440
Hey, are you okay?

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:00.520
This isn't the ocean.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.320
Arashi, this isn't the ocean!

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:06.150
The water doesn't smell of salt at all.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:10.660
What? The water around this island
isn't the ocean?

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:11.830
That's right.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.200
Then, what is it?

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.910
It's a lake, I think.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.670
That means we have a chance
of reaching another shore.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:24.250
Cut the crap! Even I know that
the biggest lake in Japan is Lake Biwa!

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.880
At Lake Biwa,
you can still see the opposite shore!

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.800
This might not be the same as the Japan
that we once knew.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:30.890
What?

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:34.310
It's hard to imagine,
but the terrain may have changed.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.180
It would be worth going out
on the boat to find out.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:39.440
What do you think, Big Sis Botan?

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:40.650
Right.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.150
Let's start by reinforcing the boat.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.860
What are you doing over there?

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.490
Chimackie has been leaving wall paintings
here and there to mark where we've been.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.790
Why don't you write your names?

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:57.330
Someone else might find this.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.760
ARASHI AOTA - FOR HANA

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.220
I'll write your name here too, Mr. Mozu.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:17.060
You know, to a small-time crook like me,
that Mozu guy looks like a hard-core thug.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:19.480
You're a small-time crook, Semimaru?

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.480
Don't you go calling me that.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.400
You said it yourself!

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.270
Oh, thank goodness.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:27.530
What? What's that about?

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.280
Nothing.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:50.010
I think the good weather will continue
for a few more days.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:52.680
You can totally trust Hotaru's forecast.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.220
She's never been wrong.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:55.890
Then, we'll leave today.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.640
Let's head northeast.

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:20.580
Search for food and water,
and gather firewood.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.910
It's the same thing,
no matter where we go.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.000
Yes.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.630
Okay, this one is safe.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:29.800
You're well on your way to becoming
a real mushroom expert.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:32.010
I'm not that good at it yet.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:35.430
Hey, food gathering squad,
can't you find us some meat?

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.300
Man, I want some meat!

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.680
Don't be ridiculous.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.600
There's no way we're still in Japan.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.850
This must be Africa or the Amazon.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.270
Right, Nat?

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:47.440
Please don't touch me.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.610
What's this?
You learned how to talk back, Nat--

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:50.820
That's enough.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:52.110
Get your hands off me!

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:56.240
Take a look. We're having meat tonight.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.820
Meat!

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:02.950
Where's Chimaki?

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.000
He was digging up rocks somewhere earlier.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:07.170
He'll show up when he gets hungry.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:08.210
But you know...

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.340
this is pretty tasty!

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.340
I'm not a big fan of this stuff.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.010
I think they're delicious.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.930
Hey! You've got no guts.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:26.100
Big Sis Botan, I've been wondering
why you said we should go northeast.

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:29.060
We were gathered in northern Kyushu,

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:32.030
so we should have been released
near the East China Sea.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:34.280
Are all of the teams near here?

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:35.860
No, we were split up.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:39.780
Team Spring is in the Kanto region
and Team Winter in Hokkaido.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.200
Team Autumn and Summer A are...

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.580
I don't really remember.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.370
Why is Summer the only one with two teams?

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:48.370
Well...

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.840
The team members had to meet
certain criteria.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:55.510
Healthy and clearheaded young people
raised in a stable home were chosen.

00:09:55.590 --> 00:10:00.970
They also had to excel in a certain field
and be physically attractive.

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:02.220
That makes no sense.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.270
I sure wasn't raised in a stable home.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:07.640
They worried about that kind of thing,

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:12.270
so they selected problem kids to make
a so-called "dropouts team."

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:15.150
They became Team Summer B.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.860
Right, I was definitely a dropout in life.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.870
The same is true for me.
I was a complete shut-in.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:26.790
I fit that, too. I did something
that hurt a lot of people.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:29.210
Damn it, this really pisses me off!

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.040
I'll show them I'm a survivor!

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:35.050
I'm no loser! Just watch!
I'll live until my hair turns gray!

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.670
That's the kind of vitality we need.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.680
Quit being so analytical!

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.510
-Hey.
-What?

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:44.310
I came across something weird.
Want to see it?

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:45.470
-What?
-What?

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:51.810
That.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:52.900
A hand?

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:54.520
I'll dive in and take a look.

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:56.690
Me too.

00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:59.150
Please be careful.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:01.570
Thanks, but don't worry about me.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.410
I used to be on the swim team.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.250
Let's follow them on the boat.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.060
If you can't dive deep enough,
then get out of there.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:29.810
That thing...

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:31.730
I've seen that dude before!

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:42.030
It's the Peace Statue!

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:43.410
This is Nagasaki!

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:50.370
<i>There are what look like the buried ruins
of a city along the bottom.</i>

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:52.710
Nagasaki...

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.630
is at the bottom of the sea.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:00.670
If Nagasaki is under the sea,
then all the other cities are too.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:10.390
Now that we know we're in Nagasaki,
our destination is clear.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:13.350
We're going to Fuji.
Mt. Bungo Fuji in Oita Prefecture.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:15.360
Also known as Mt. Yufu.
That's where we'll go.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:23.070
<i>Supplies were left in storage shelters
on Japan's seven regional Fuji mountains.</i>

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.160
It doesn't look tasty, but it's edible.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:30.580
Mr. Mozu,
let me help you skin and clean it.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.210
Arashi...

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:35.710
First, strip off the skin
and then remove the intestines.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:37.170
Right.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:44.470
Hey, if you can't handle it, don't do it.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.800
Your hands are trembling.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:48.810
I have to be able to do
at least this much.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.520
<i>If Hana were here,</i>

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:54.060
<i>I would do whatever it took to feed her,</i>

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:55.850
<i>blood and guts be damned.</i>

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:01.440
<i>After that, Arashi stopped talking much.</i>

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:07.990
From what I was told, there's a landmark
on Mt. Yufu's south side.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.870
The storage shelter should be
right beneath it.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:13.750
Just a landmark?
Don't you have a map or something?

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.040
Did you forget the terrain has
completely changed?

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:18.500
Having a map won't do us any good.

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:20.550
Then what the hell should we do?

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.590
Oh, boy. There she goes,
falling down again.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:27.640
You're such a damn klutz, Natsu!

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:29.350
I'm really sorry.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:30.430
Are you okay?

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:31.930
Yes.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:35.890
There's some kind of statue down here.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.980
A statue of Vairocana, perhaps?

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:41.900
The carving is pretty rough,
but it has a lot of character.

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:49.910
Here it is.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:51.780
This is the entrance.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:53.700
Help me get it open.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:13:59.170
Let's check it out.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.720
Rice! There's rice here!

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.970
I found flour and sugar!

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:14.520
There's medicine, too!

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:15.980
Some fabric and tools as well.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:17.060
And seeds.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:18.980
-All right!
-Yes!

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:23.780
Hold up. Food I can understand.
But seeds? What's up with that?

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.150
You want me to farm?

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:27.110
Exactly.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.070
What?

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:31.530
Not just farm,
but every aspect of agriculture.

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:35.370
Fishing, forestry, hunting,
raising livestock, woodworking, crafting.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:39.120
In other words, you'll have to live a life
of complete self-sufficiency.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:42.210
What? You expect me to stoop
to being self-sufficient?

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:45.000
Well, excuse me!
Some of us used to be farmers!

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.670
Seriously? You sure don't act
like a country bumpkin.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:51.340
For now, we'll make this our base camp
and settle in here for a while.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:52.850
Excuse me.

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:54.350
What's up, Chimackie?

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:58.680
There's a place I want to visit,
so I'm leaving for a few days.

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:01.850
You want to see your hometown
of Kumamoto, right?

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:20.250
So everything that Big Sis Botan told us
turned out to be true?

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:29.550
Kumamoto should be around here.

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:30.590
What?

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.800
Since I was a kid,

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:35.720
I was forced to sketch Kumamoto Castle

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:38.470
until I was sick of it.

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:41.730
What about your house?

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:46.320
It's straight that way,
about a 15-minute walk from the castle.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:49.900
Everybody is gone now.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:56.780
Why are you two crying?

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.310
What happened?

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:20.600
He tried to claim all of the food stores
for himself, so we tied him up.

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:21.770
Damn it!

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:23.480
So, how did it go?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:24.900
Well...

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.150
I see.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.530
Big Sis Botan,
will we be staying here for a while?

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:33.610
I think so.
The conditions here are pretty good.

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:37.200
Okay. Then I'll go check on my home
as well.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:38.450
Stay here with everyone.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.290
Your home? You're from Tokyo, right?

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.920
Yes. There's someone
I have to try and see, no matter what.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:49.090
Right.
I can tell it's pointless to stop you.

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:52.260
Go ahead, but make sure
you take enough supplies with you.

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:53.510
Thank you.

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:56.140
I'll go too.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:00.970
I'll go with you.

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:02.770
My home was nearby, in Saitama.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:04.770
Is it all right if I join you?

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.860
I realize I'll get in your way,

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.190
and be a burden, but...

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:11.610
You're not a burden.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:15.030
But still, it's going to be dangerous.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:16.990
Please!

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:19.700
Okay.

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:22.290
There's someone
you want to see too, right?

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.960
I understand. Let's go together.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:26.000
Right.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.460
<i>The person I want to see
is right in front of me.</i>

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.100
A ship? Everyone, there's a ship!

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:44.810
A ship?

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:46.690
Really?

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:48.560
We're saved!

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:49.690
Hey!

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:51.150
Hello!

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:52.650
Over here!

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:54.070
Look over here!

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:56.030
-Please help us!
-Hey!

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.200
-Hello!
-Hey!

00:17:58.280 --> 00:17:59.490
Somebody!

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.410
It doesn't look like
they'll be helping us.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.500
There's nobody on that ship.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:12.420
It's abandoned
and it's just floating around.

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:14.670
Oh, but look!

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:18.970
That's a Japanese ship, right?

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:23.430
He's right! If there's a ship,
we must be close to the shore.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:24.890
Yes. That's true.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.600
We're really in Japan!

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:28.020
We made it.

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:29.600
We found our way back.

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:36.740
-What? What's that?
-Not sure.

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:38.950
That must be...

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:46.450
Yokohama Landmark Tower and hotel.

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:52.290
That's impossible.

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:01.260
Of the seven Fuji mountains,
the closest to us is Mt. Kobe Fuji.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.470
<i>If we can find it, let's check it out.</i>

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:09.980
Are you okay, Ms. Iwashimizu?

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.690
You have to tell me
if this is too tough for you.

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:15.730
I'm fine.

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:17.190
I'm not mad at you.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.150
It's just that, if you can't walk,
we can't go anywhere.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:22.110
I'm fine, really.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:26.120
Then we had better massage our feet.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.450
Right.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:37.590
<i>I've come really close to asking him
if I should have stayed behind.</i>

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:40.880
<i>But I know asking that is
the absolute worst thing I can do.</i>

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:45.550
<i>I'm getting used to outdoor survival.</i>

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:49.770
This would be perfect as toilet paper.
It's big and soft.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:52.060
Okay, I'll gather a bunch of them to keep.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:55.400
It sure is hard to start a fire.

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:57.730
Semimaru was pretty good at it, though.

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:02.740
If you're bored, I'll lend you my book.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:05.950
Oh, I've read that before.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.240
But only the first half.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.500
Really? What did you think?

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.870
Well, it was interesting.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:15.880
But I really hated the main character.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:18.880
I mean, when the kittens were born,

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:21.470
he killed them
because he thought they were annoying.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.430
Don't you think that's the worst?

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:28.810
You're pretty funny, Ms. Iwashimizu.
It cracks me up.

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:30.270
What? I am?

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:32.850
Sometimes you blurt out your opinion
loud and clear.

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:35.060
Well...

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:40.940
What? Aren't those yams?

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:46.910
Look!

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:48.490
Wow! Nice find!

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.620
I'm glad you came with me.

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:54.750
What?

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:58.130
If I were alone, I probably
would have been too scared to keep going.

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:02.630
Something is coming.

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:07.300
Ants! I got swarmed by ants!
Get them off me! Hurry!

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:09.140
Semimaru? Why are you here?

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.890
Who cares? Just hurry up
and get them off me! I'm begging you!

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.770
I can't stand to touch bugs.

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:16.900
-What's so scary about ants?
-Hurry up and get them off!

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:19.440
Never mind that! Just hurry up
and get them off me, damn it!

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:21.320
Why did you follow us?

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:25.450
Because Big Sis was giving me a hard time,
and I hate staying in one place for long.

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:27.490
So, where did you use to live?

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:29.660
You're worried too, right? Where is it?

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:31.620
Hamamatsu.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.210
A bridge?

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:36.080
Are there other people here?

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:37.080
Well...

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:51.810
People...

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:54.730
Excuse me.

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:56.390
Who are you?

00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:01.020
Get out of here!

00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:14.660
What's this?

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:16.910
Who the hell are you?
